Key Findings & Results Summary
1. Observational Cohort & Matching Balance
Unadjusted Cohort: Significant selection imbalance; patients in the SGLT2i arm exhibited higher baseline comorbidity counts.
Post-PSM Balance: Propensity score matching yielded 100% covariate balance across all clinical features, reducing Standardized Mean Differences (SMD) below the standard 0.10 threshold.
2. Base-Case Economic Model (20-Year Horizon)
Standard Care Total Discounted Cost: $23,942.10 | Discounted QALYs: 6.821
Novel SGLT2i Total Discounted Cost: $28,145.20 | Discounted QALYs: 6.981
Incremental Cost (ΔC): $4,203.10
Incremental Effectiveness (ΔE): 0.160 QALYs
Base-Case ICER: $26,269.38 / QALY gained
3. Decision Assessment
At standard Health Technology Assessment (HTA) Willingness-to-Pay (WTP) thresholds of $50,000/QALY and $100,000/QALY, Novel SGLT2i therapy is highly cost-effective.
